+  "title": "Recap: Obligation in the Past",
   "sections": [
     {
       "type": "text",
-      "title": "The Structural Mechanism",
-      "content": "Deontic modal structures articulate statutory and constitutional obligations that the executive branch must respect, or prohibited actions: `nem foszthatja meg a bíróságot a felülvizsgálati jogtól` (must not deprive the court of judicial review), `nem csorbíthatja a hatásköröket önkényesen` (must not curtail competences arbitrarily), `köteles garantálni az érdemi normakontrollt` (is obligated to guarantee merit-based norm control), `tiszteletben kell tartania a jogállami határokat` (must respect rule-of-law boundaries)."
